# Database Area Instructions

- Read existing schema and migration history before editing.
- Prefer expand/migrate/contract and backward-compatible releases.
- Define invariants, constraints, indexes, lock/performance impact, data volume, backfill, and validation.
- Migrations and backfills must be idempotent/resumable when practical.
- Writing migration code is not approval to run it against production.
- Destructive changes require backup/recovery evidence and a human-approved runbook.
